Changelog: 15-11-2026 23:08:55

Added. Boot Command Line shows the kernel command line one argument per row, with what each argument does, and
edits it there: a double click edits a row, Add puts a known argument (or an empty row) under the selected one,
Remove, Up and Down work on the selected row, and the line Save changes writes shows below the table. All settings
lists every argument the PS5 Linux command lines use, with its values. A list beside the boxes also opens the
fallback lines on the loader's partition (cmdline.txt.m2, cmdline.txt.usb), each saved with its own dated backup.
An info symbol beside All settings links the wiki's PS5 Linux boot partition chapter.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 20:10:01

Added. Console Helpers, small windows for one job each that come with the suite: Test Extras (the optional tools
Board Test's tests use, which are there and which tests use them, installed per group with Board Test's own install-
requirements.sh), MangoHud Config (opens or makes ~/.config/MangoHud/MangoHud.conf to edit and save, sets the FPS
log Board Test reads and makes its folder, deletes logs older than 30 days), Game Memory Map (vm.max_map_count in
/etc/sysctl.d), Persistent Journal (/var/log/journal) and Boot Command Line (edits /boot/efi/cmdline.txt, the kernel
command line the PS5 loader starts Linux with). Game Memory Map and Persistent Journal ask for the password with
pkexec, turn on only what is off and turn off only what they turned on. Boot Command Line's Save changes warns that
it changes the boot settings of PS5 Linux and asks Yes (save), No (drop the edits) or Cancel (keep editing); it
saves only one line with root=, after a dated backup of the file beside it, and reads a file your user may not read
after your password. ps5-helpers opens the list of helpers, ps5-helpers <key> one helper.
